From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] psu: log unmatched discovered devices at debug level

PSU hwmon devices can be present before their Entity-Manager configuration
is available. Configuration changes trigger another scan, and an unmatched
device during discovery is not a sensor read failure. Keep this diagnostic
at debug level without changing matching, rescans or genuine error handling.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
+++ b/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
@@ -527,9 +527,11 @@
         }
         if (interfacePath == nullptr)
         {
-            // To avoid this error message, add your export map entry,
-            // from Entity Manager, to sensorTypes at the top of this file.
-            lg2::error("failed to find match for '{NAME}'", "NAME", deviceName);
+            // The hwmon device may precede its Entity-Manager configuration.
+            // Configuration changes trigger another scan; this is not a read
+            // failure of an already configured PSU sensor.
+            lg2::debug("Skipping PSU device '{NAME}': no matching configuration",
+                       "NAME", deviceName);
             continue;
         }
 
